# Phase 2 — Network Infrastructure Configuration
**Homelab Project | github.com/thelogansmith/Homelab**

**Objective:** Configure the MikroTik RB4011iGS+ edge router and TP-Link TL-SG1016DE managed switch to establish VLAN segmentation, WAN connectivity, NAT, and traffic distribution to all Proxmox nodes.

**Definition of done:**
- MikroTik WAN interface receiving ISP DHCP lease
- OPNsense WAN receiving DHCP lease from MikroTik (`10.0.10.2`)
- VLAN 99 devices receiving DHCP from MikroTik (`192.168.99.x`)
- TP-Link switch trunking VLANs 10/20/40/50/99 to all Proxmox nodes
- VMs on pve-nuc1 and pve-nuc2 receiving DHCP leases from OPNsense on correct VLANs

---

## Architecture Overview

The lab uses an intentional double-NAT design. The MikroTik sits at the network edge, handles WAN connectivity, and provides the outer NAT layer. OPNsense (VM 100 on pve-srv1) acts as the inner firewall and gateway for all trusted VLANs. VLAN 99 (Untrusted/IoT) is the exception — it is fully MikroTik-owned and never touches OPNsense.

### VLAN Summary

| VLAN | Name | Subnet | Gateway | Managed By |
|------|------|--------|---------|------------|
| 10 | Management | `10.10.10.0/24` | `10.10.10.1` | OPNsense |
| 20 | Internal | `192.168.20.0/24` | `192.168.20.1` | OPNsense |
| 40 | Personal | `10.40.40.0/24` | `10.40.40.1` | OPNsense |
| 50 | DMZ | `172.16.50.0/24` | `172.16.50.1` | OPNsense |
| 99 | Untrusted/IoT | `192.168.99.0/24` | `192.168.99.1` | MikroTik |

### MikroTik RB4011 — Physical Port Assignment

| Port | Connected Device | Role |
|------|-----------------|------|
| ether1 | ISP Modem/ONT | WAN — DHCP client upstream |
| ether2 | MikroTik cAP ax WAP | Trunk — VLAN 40 + VLAN 99 tagged |
| ether3 | Gaming PC | Trunk — VLAN 10 + VLAN 40 tagged (Windows config deferred — see Step 6) |
| ether4 | pve-srv1 (vmbr0) | OPNsense WAN transit — `10.0.10.0/24` |
| ether9 | TP-Link switch | Primary trunk — VLANs 10/20/40/50/99 |
| ether10 | TP-Link switch | Redundant trunk — VLANs 10/20/40/50/99 (future LACP) |

